{"event":"plan_loaded","task_count":5,"tasks":[{"id":"cli-entry-point","deps":[],"files":["unitconv/cli.py","unitconv/__main__.py"],"difficulty":"easy","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b"},{"id":"tests","deps":["unit-registry","conversion-engine","cli-entry-point"],"files":["tests/test_converter.py"],"difficulty":"hard","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-27b"},{"id":"unit-registry","deps":[],"files":["unitconv/__init__.py","unitconv/unit_registry.py"],"difficulty":"easy","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b"},{"id":"integrate-verify","deps":["unit-registry","conversion-engine","cli-entry-point","tests"],"files":[],"difficulty":"hard","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-27b"},{"id":"conversion-engine","deps":[],"files":["unitconv/converter.py"],"difficulty":"hard","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-27b"}],"raw_plan_json":"{\"subtasks\":[{\"id\":\"unit-registry\",\"description\":\"Define all unit categories (length, weight, temperature, data-size) with base factors and temperature offsets\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"model\":\"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b\",\"depends_on\":[],\"files\":[\"unitconv/__init__.py\",\"unitconv/unit_registry.py\"]},{\"id\":\"conversion-engine\",\"description\":\"Conversion logic with validation (category match, numeric check, absolute zero), precision rounding at end only\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"model\":\"qwen/qwen3.6-27b\",\"depends_on\":[],\"files\":[\"unitconv/converter.py\"]},{\"id\":\"cli-entry-point\",\"description\":\"## Subtask Spec: CLI Entry Point (`cli.py`)\\n\\n### Files Owned\\n- `unitconv/cli.py` — argparse setup, subcommand handlers, main() entry point\\n- `unitconv/__main__.py` — one-liner calling `cli.main()` for `python -m unitconv` support\\n\\n### Function Signatures & Key Logic\\n\\n```python\\n# cli.py\\ndef build_parser() -> ArgumentParser: ...\\ndef handle_list(args: Namespace) -> None: ...\\ndef handle_convert(args: Namespace) -> None: ...\\ndef main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int: ...\\n```\\n\\n**`build_parser()`**: Create `ArgumentParser(prog=\\\"unitconv\\\")`. Add subparsers with `dest=\\\"command\\\"`, required=True. Subparser `\\\"list\\\"` takes positional `category` (choices from registry keys). Subparser `\\\"convert\\\"` takes positionals `value` (type=float), `from_unit`, `to_unit`, and optional `--precision` (int, default=2, metavar=\\\"N\\\").\\n\\n**`handle_list(args)`**: Import the unit registry; print each supported unit for `args.category` on its own line. Exit 0.\\n\\n**`handle_convert(args)`**: Validate: (1) both units exist in same category — if not, error with valid-unit list and exit 2; (2) value is finite (`math.isfinite`) — else \\\"not a number\\\" exit 2; (3) precision ≥ 0 — else \\\"invalid precision\\\" exit 2. Delegate to the conversion engine (imported from `unitconv.convert`), round only at final output step. Print result: if precision == 0, format as integer (`f\\\"{result:.0f}\\\"`); otherwise `f\\\"{result:.{precision}f}\\\"`. Exit 0 on success.\\n\\n**`main(argv=None)`**: Call `build_parser().parse_args(argv)`, dispatch via `args.command` (\\\"list\\\" → handle_list, \\\"convert\\\" → handle_convert). Return exit code (0 or 2).\\n\\n### Edge Cases to Handle\\n- Cross-category units: detect by checking both resolve to the same category key; error with list of valid units for each.\\n- Case-insensitive unit matching: normalize `from_unit`/`to_unit` via `.lower()` before lookup.\\n- Same-unit conversion is allowed (identity).\\n- Zero value is valid in all categories.\\n- Negative Kelvin/Rankine: the conversion engine must reject; CLI surfaces that error with exit 2.\\n\\n### Tests Must Check (`tests/test_cli.py`)\\n1. `convert 100 celsius fahrenheit` → stdout \\\"212.0\\\", rc=0\\n2. `convert 32 fahrenheit celsius` → \\\"0.0\\\", rc=0\\n3. `convert -40 celsius fahrenheit` → \\\"-40.0\\\", rc=0\\n4. `convert 1 meter foot --precision 2` → \\\"3.28\\\", rc=0\\n5. `convert 1 meter foot --precision 0` → \\\"3\\\" (no decimal), rc=0\\n6. `convert 1 meter foot --precision -1` → error msg, rc=2\\n7. `convert abc meter foot` → argparse float parse error, rc!=0\\n8. `convert 5 meter kilogram` → cross-category error + valid units listed, rc=2\\n9. `convert 5 meter unknown_unit` → unit-not-found error + valid length units, rc=2\\n10. `convert 1 meter meter` → \\\"1.0\\\", rc=0 (identity)\\n11. `list length` → prints all length units, one per line, rc=0\\n12. No args → usage printed, rc!=0\\n13. Case-insensitive: `convert 1 METER FOOT` works same as lowercase\",\"difficulty\":\"easy\",\"model\":\"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b\",\"depends_on\":[],\"files\":[\"unitconv/cli.py\",\"unitconv/__main__.py\"]},{\"id\":\"tests\",\"description\":\"Pytest covering conversion matrix, validation errors, edge cases (absolute zero, cross-category, precision), and CLI behavior\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"model\":\"qwen/qwen3.6-27b\",\"depends_on\":[\"unit-registry\",\"conversion-engine\",\"cli-entry-point\"],\"files\":[\"tests/test_converter.py\"]},{\"id\":\"integrate-verify\",\"description\":\"Run pytest, fix all failures until green, then run main command once to confirm it starts\",\"difficulty\":\"hard\",\"model\":\"qwen/qwen3.6-27b\",\"depends_on\":[\"unit-registry\",\"conversion-engine\",\"cli-entry-point\",\"tests\"],\"files\":[]}],\"integration\":\"python3 -m pytest && python3 -m unitconv convert 100 celsius fahrenheit\"}","ts":"2026-06-27T10:07:39.608538+00:00","run_id":"swarm-20260627-095923778","seq":3}
